[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: High-Level Requirements
UID: HLR-DOC
VERSION: 1.0

[GRAMMAR]
ELEMENTS:
- TAG: REQUIREMENT
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: RATIONALE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  RELATIONS:
  - TYPE: Parent

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-001
TITLE: Markdown Output Format
STATEMENT: The system shall generate test documentation in Markdown format.
RATIONALE: Markdown is widely supported and human-readable.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYSREQ-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-002
TITLE: AsciiDoc Output Format
STATEMENT: The system shall generate test documentation in AsciiDoc format.
RATIONALE: AsciiDoc provides advanced formatting capabilities for technical documentation.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYSREQ-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-003
TITLE: Tera Template Engine
STATEMENT: The system shall use the Tera template engine for rendering templates.
RATIONALE: Tera provides Jinja2-like syntax familiar to many users.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYSREQ-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-004
TITLE: JSON Schema Validation
STATEMENT: The system shall use JSON Schema specification for validating input data.
RATIONALE: JSON Schema is a standard and widely-adopted validation approach.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYSREQ-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-005
TITLE: Container Schema Validation
STATEMENT: The system shall validate container-level data against a user-provided JSON schema.
RATIONALE: Container data structure may vary between projects.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYSREQ-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-006
TITLE: Test Case Schema Validation
STATEMENT: The system shall validate each test case data file against its type-specific JSON schema.
RATIONALE: Different verification methods may have different data structures.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYSREQ-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-007
TITLE: Test Verification Method
STATEMENT: The system shall support test verification method with dedicated schema and template.
RATIONALE: Testing is the primary verification method for most requirements.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYSREQ-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-008
TITLE: Analysis Verification Method
STATEMENT: The system shall support analysis verification method with dedicated schema and template.
RATIONALE: Some requirements are verified through analysis rather than testing.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYSREQ-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-009
TITLE: Demonstration Verification Method
STATEMENT: The system shall support demonstration verification method with dedicated schema and template.
RATIONALE: Demonstration is appropriate for user-facing functionality verification.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYSREQ-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-010
TITLE: Inspection Verification Method
STATEMENT: The system shall support inspection verification method with dedicated schema and template.
RATIONALE: Inspection is used for design and documentation verification.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYSREQ-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-011
TITLE: CLI Arguments
STATEMENT: The system shall accept command-line arguments for specifying input files and output options.
RATIONALE: CLI arguments enable flexible invocation from scripts and build systems.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYSREQ-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-012
TITLE: Exit Codes
STATEMENT: The system shall return appropriate exit codes for success and different error conditions.
RATIONALE: Exit codes enable automated error detection in scripts and CI/CD pipelines.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYSREQ-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-013
TITLE: Requirements Aggregation
STATEMENT: The system shall aggregate requirements coverage from test cases into a summary report.
RATIONALE: Aggregated view helps identify coverage gaps.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYSREQ-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-014
TITLE: Container Template
STATEMENT: The system shall render a container template that includes test plan metadata and aggregated test cases.
RATIONALE: Container template provides the overall structure of the documentation.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYSREQ-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-015
TITLE: Test Case Templates
STATEMENT: The system shall render individual test case templates based on verification method type.
RATIONALE: Each verification method may require different formatting and content.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYSREQ-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-016
TITLE: Custom Template Filters
STATEMENT: The system shall provide custom Tera filters for common text transformations.
RATIONALE: Custom filters reduce template complexity and enable reusable text processing logic.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYSREQ-002
